      "standard_id": "EML-2.2.0",
      "name": "Ecological Metadata Language (EML)",
      "description": "A community-maintained XML metadata specification (EML 2.2.0) for documenting ecological, earth and environmental research data and related resources. Covers dataset- and resource-level bibliographic metadata, modules for dataset structure (entities, attributes, dataTable, spatial raster/vector), discovery and interpretation fields (party, coverage, methods, project), semantic annotations, internationalization, validation rules, and support for data papers and licensing."
    }
